From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:22:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Explain failed thread checks in the log

A failed thread check logs only the reason, the thread and the
position, and server owners cannot tell which plugin is at fault or
what it should do instead. Add a line to the log message with the
plugin and the method it called, the kind of thread (global region,
another region, no region), and the Folia API to use for blocks and
chunks or for entities. For plugins in compatibility mode it says why
the region loan did not apply. Without a plugin on the stack it asks
for a report. The exception message is unchanged. The thread context
names the global region instead of {null}.

